WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.768
-Our next guest is
a very funny comedian

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.137
you know from her work
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.605
which returns this week
live on NBC and Peacock,

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.441
with host Dakota Johnson

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.076
and musical guest
Justin Timberlake.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:12.912
Please welcome to the show
Punkie Johnson, everybody!

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:15.614
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:18.984
[ Mid-tempo music plays ]

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:27.660
♪♪

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:28.961
Welcome to the show, Punkie.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.563
-What's up, y'all?
What's up, Seth?

00:00:30.629 --> 00:00:32.465
How you doing?
I'm happy to be here.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.067
-I appreciate you making time
on a Tuesday.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.868
I know what a busy day it is.
-Oh, absolutely.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:36.970
We got Write Night tonight.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.270
-You got a writing night
tonight?

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:39.872
It's gonna be a long night.
-Yes, it is.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:43.543
I have heard this story that
early in your time at "SNL,"

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.179
you actually, uh -- you kind of
pulled a power move.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.514
There was somebody who could not
get into the "SNL" afterparty.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.717
-Oh, yeah. [ Laughs ]
-And we have a photo.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:53.118
And This is Travis Kelce.
They would not let him in.

00:00:53.185 --> 00:00:54.987
-Right, right, right, right,
right.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.456
-Now, what really happened?
Is it true that at the door

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:58.758
they just didn't know
who Travis was?

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:00.359
-The crazy thing is,
he had came to the show.

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:01.728
We saw him at the show.
And then he goes

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.530
to the afterparty,
and he's just looking.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.931
And I was like,
"Oh, that's Travis Kelce."

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:07.300
And they're sitting up there --
they're like,

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.535
"You can't get in, bro.
You're not on the list."

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.003
And I'm sitting up there like,

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.571
"Why isn't he
listing his résumé?

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:15.007
'Cause I'm on 'SNL.'
I'm, like, D-list celebrity."

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.475
I would have been
like, "I'm on 'SNL'!

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:17.976
I know Lorne Michaels!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:20.179
But he was just sitting up
there, just being so innocent,

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.981
like, "Oh, my God,
should I call someone?"

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.750
So I went over there,
and I was like,

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.984
"This is a Super Bowl champion!

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:30.290
He is daggone the greatest
tight end in the daggone NFL!"

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.357
I was saying everything
he should have said.

00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:33.993
-Yeah.
-And I was like,

00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:36.029
"He's on my list!
Come on, Travis!"

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.930
[ Laughter ]
And -- And then

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.699
I guess we became,
like, friends.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.600
I made him take pict--
Well, forceful friends.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.169
I'm like, "You're gonna
take pictures with me

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.537
every time you see me."
-Yep.

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:47.106
-"I'm gonna be
heavily a part of your life.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.641
We're having children
together.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.711
Like, "You owe me for this party
forever, bro."

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:52.845
-That would have been
very embarrassing.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.346
This is a very cool picture.

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:56.482
If it had just been him standing
outside a party, very lame.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.716
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.652
-Uh, what --
I always like to ask,

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.320
where were you
when you got the call

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.289
that you were hired on "SNL"?

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.724
-Oh, man.
So, it was very shaky.

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:08.227
You know, this job, they be
playing a lot of mind games.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.729
-They do that.
-They like,

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:11.364
"We gonna call you on --"
They're like,

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.966
"Lorne Michaels is gonna
call you on a Friday..."

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.600
-Uh-huh.
-"...if you got the job."

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.502
Friday done came and gone.
Lorne ain't calling.

00:02:16.568 --> 00:02:17.703
I'm like, "I ain't get the job."

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.204
They called me Saturday morning,
"Alright,

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:21.373
he gonna call you today
for sure if you got the job."

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.543
Lorne ain't call.
I'm like, "I ain't got the job."

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:29.181
So, Sunday is Tom Brady
is playing his first game

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:30.917
in the NFC with the Bucs...
-Yeah.

00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:33.352
-,,,against my team,
New Orleans Saints.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.921
And I'm like -- Drew Brees
is giving it to him, too.

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:37.757
I'm like, "Yeah,
we run the NFC!"

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:40.025
And it's a big old family party.
We so excited.

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:42.161
I'm drinking, I'm --
you know I'm celebrating

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.397
the fact that I got that far
in the audition process.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:46.198
I'm like, "I didn't make it.
Whatever."

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.668
And then, as I'm taking a shot,
Lorne calls.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.469
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.304
By this point,
I'm like, "Oh, God."

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.106
You know what I'm saying?
So, I answer the phone.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:59.245
I'm like, "Hey!
Yes, this is Punkie. Hi!"

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:01.080
And then he has this
long conversation with me.

00:03:01.146 --> 00:03:02.482
I don't know what
he's talking about,

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.684
'cause I'm in a trance
at this moment,

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:07.419
trying to figure out how
to not let this man know

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:08.688
I've been drinking,

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.857
watching Drew Brees
beat up on Tom Brady.

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:12.892
And, um, at the end
of the conversation,

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.327
he's like, "Yo,
come be on the cast.

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:16.095
You got the job."
I'm like, "Yo, what's up?"

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.730
Then he said,
"Oh, pack your bags.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.933
You leave tomorrow."
I'm like, "It's 6:00 p.m."

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.967
[ Laughter ]
I'm like, "What kind of job..."

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.903
-You were like,
"I'm gonna start celebrating."

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.771
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-Your, mom, Mary,

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:26.939
who was on the show.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.340
-Yeah. Yeah yeah yeah,
yeah, yeah.

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:29.842
-A lovely picture
of you and your mom.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:33.112
And when you packed those bags
to come to New York City,

00:03:33.178 --> 00:03:35.781
she put a couple of pictures
in your suitcase,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.583
with a couple of notes.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.984
She put some pictures
and some notes.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.987
Pictures of us and, like,
stuff, like, you know,

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:43.456
"We proud of you.
You made it.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.691
'Live from New York,
it's Punkie Johnson!'"

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.092
All that stuff. Yeah, cute.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:49.362 line:91%
And then under that, um,
[Chuckles] --

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.463
under that, she was like,
"But I got an invoice

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.899
of all the money you owe me
from the time you was born."

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:56.769
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.872
"And now is the time for you
to start paying me back.

00:03:59.938 --> 00:04:02.207
You finally -- You finally
on the road to recovery."

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:04.410
I'm like -- She's like,
"You owe me for your life."

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.945
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:08.481
I'm like,
"I ain't asked to be here.

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:10.683
How do I owe you?"
But --

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.552
-She's gotten used
to the finer things?

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:15.488
-She has. I've been taking --
She's been fine-dining.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:17.156
I've been putting her
on first class

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.091
all around the world now.
Now she bougie.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.326
[ Laughter ]
She's mad bougie.

00:04:21.393 --> 00:04:23.129
So now, like,
she called me one time,

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:25.064
I was getting her
to come out here to New York,

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:26.932
and it was on a specific date,
and she was like,

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:28.767
"Unh-unh,
they only got comfort.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:32.505
'Cause everything was sold out.
I was like, "Well, Ma,

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.873
you got to ride comfort,
because I need shoes."

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.241
Like, "I'm gonna have
to come the day after

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.443
or the day before, because..."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.379
"this comfort --
this three-row seat stuff

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.114
ain't gonna work for me."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.750
-She got used to it.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.317
-I mean, you know,
once you get them accustomed

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:47.086
to a certain way of life,
you got to keep it rolling.

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:49.322
-Now you have a
less-than-bougie ritual

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:53.226
after the afterparty.
-Oh. Super trashy, yeah.

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:54.894
[ Laughter ]
But everybody think it's trashy,

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:58.063
and I don't.
After every "SNL" party,

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.199
I got to hit up some Taco Bell.
-Okay.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.702
I gotta do it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:05.404
-Now, the "SNL" party
will move around.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.805
The afterparty
is different every week.

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:08.674
Do you then know the locations
of the closest Taco Bell

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.108
when you're leaving?

00:05:10.175 --> 00:05:14.013
-So, I be a little bit
under the weather intoxicatedly,

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.715
so my driver
always knows the location.

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:17.950
-Great. That's good.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.618
-My driver always know.
"Taco Bell?"

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:21.720
I'm like, "Taco Bell.
You know what's going on."

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:24.356
So I go to Taco Bell.
The people at Taco Bell know me.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.626
I be -- I be tipping them.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.597
Because I always go
with an entourage,

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.198
and it's always
some foolishness.

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:35.701
I'm like, "Man, take this 50,
my dawg,"

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.136
and it be all good.
-That's good.

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:39.404
You've done a lot of
really great musical things

00:05:39.471 --> 00:05:40.606
on the show.
-Yeah.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:43.309
-You did a wonderful rap
with Keke Palmer.

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:45.144
And rapping was actually
something you were gonna

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.779
pursue back in the day.
-Ha-ha!

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:50.749
-You have yourself a rap name.
-I did. I sucked.

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:52.785
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.755
-But, [Chuckles] I mean,
I thought I was good at rapping

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:57.656
until I heard other rappers,
and I was like,

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.425
"Nah, let me -- let me
just stick to being goofy."

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:00.993
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.963
So, my rap name was J. Willy.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.298
It wasn't even hard.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:08.567
It was just, you know,
just it was just goofy.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.704
So I was like, "Nah, just go be
a comedian, bro. You good."

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.906
-Well, I'm glad you made
the choice you did.

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:16.008
It has been a fantastic season
for you so far.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.476
And it's been great
having you here tonight.

00:06:17.542 --> 00:06:18.944
Thank you so much.
-Absolutely.

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.847
Thank y'all so much,
-That's Punkie Johnson.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.582
"SNL"returns this week,
live on NBC and Peacock,

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:26.152
with host Dakota Johnson,
musical guest Justin Timberlake.

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:27.954
We'll be right back
with Brad Meltzer.

